## 📊 Direct Comparison: while vs for Loops
To help you choose the right tool for your automation scripts, look at how their capabilities differ:

| Action / Capability | while Loop | for Loop |
|---|---|---|
| Execution Length | Unknown / Dynamic (Runs until conditions change) | Known / Fixed (Runs once per item in a list) |
| Best suited for... | Handling API limits, pagination, and retries | Fuzzing specific wordlists or payload lists |
| Risk of crashing script | High (If the exit condition is never met, it loops forever) | Low (It naturally ends when the list is finished) |
| Can use break and continue? | Yes | Yes |

